course: dictionary
lesson: 10707
title: Untidy and its meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Untidy means messy, with things not in their right places. A room with clothes on the floor and books in a heap is untidy. You can say «Your room is untidy, please tidy it.» Tidy is the opposite: things are in order.
explain: Untidy can be compared: untidy, untidier, untidiest. «My desk is untidy, but Sam's is untidier.» «The attic is the untidiest room in the house.» Add -ier or -iest to compare things.
explain: Untidy is not only about rooms. It can describe handwriting that is hard to read, or floors covered in things. An untidy person often leaves things messy. To check a meaning, swap in your own word: does «messy» still make sense in the sentence? If it does, you have it.
fact: Untidy means messy, with things not in their right places.
fact: An untidy person often leaves things messy.
fact: «Untidy» can be compared: untidy, untidier, untidiest.
fact: «Tousled» is a close word: it describes hair that is messy and not smoothed down, as in Badger's «rough and touzled».
fact: Real house mice build untidy nests inside walls, under floors and behind cupboards, out of shredded paper, cloth and fluff.
exercise: «Your room is untidy, please tidy it.» What does untidy mean? | *Messy, with things not in their right places | Very clean and shiny | Quiet and calm | Hungry
exercise: «Her handwriting is untidier than mine.» Whose handwriting is harder to read? | *Hers | Both are neat | Neither, they are the same | Mine
exercise: «The attic is the untidiest room in the house.» Which word compares the most? | untidier | untidy | *untidiest | tidy
test: Untidy floors can make people trip. Why are they risky? | The room gets colder | *People can trip over things lying on the floor | The floor becomes too shiny to walk on | Only pets can use them
test: Badger arrives muddy and «rough and touzled». What does touzled mean here? | Wet with rain | *Untidy and messy | Happy and calm | Clean and washed
exam: A mouse builds «an untidy nest of fluff inside the wall». What does untidy suggest about the nest? | *Messy, with bits thrown together and not arranged neatly | Built by a bird from twigs | Neat, round and smooth like a ball | Hidden under the sea
